# Handle IDE indexing ("dumb mode")

IntelliJ's code intelligence tools depend on a background index. During indexing (after project open, dependency changes, or large VCS operations), the IDE enters "dumb mode" where most Index tools return errors or incomplete results.

## When tools fail unexpectedly

Call `ide_index_status` (Index server):
- `isDumbMode: true` → indexing in progress, wait and retry
- `isDumbMode: false` → index is ready, the failure has another cause

## When to proactively check

- At the start of a batch of Index operations (find class, find references, type hierarchy, etc.)
- After `ide_sync_files` on many files
- After opening a project or switching branches

## Recovery

If `isDumbMode` is true, wait a few seconds and re-check. Do not retry Index tools repeatedly during dumb mode — they will continue to return stale results until indexing completes.

GeneralIDE tools (`build_project`, `open_file_in_editor`, `execute_terminal_command`) are generally unaffected by dumb mode.
